Inspect existing Foundry State Stores and manage JSON object items.

Select a store once, or pass --store on individual item commands. Store selection
is saved per project endpoint and agent, independently of protocol and version.
These commands do not create stores or resume, steer, or stop agent work.

Usage
  azd ai agent state-stores [command]

Available Commands
  items  : Read, replace, and delete items in an existing State Store.
  list   : List one page of existing State Stores.
  select : Validate and save the active store, or choose one interactively.
  show   : Show the named store or the active store.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for state-stores
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
    azd ai agent state-stores list
    azd ai agent state-stores select checkpoints/run-42

Use azd ai agent state-stores [command] --help to view examples and more information about a specific command.
